# --- dashboard readings around probe A (operator-supplied, 2026-10-15) ---
dashboard_before=392s   (R0, supplied before the probe was bought)
dashboard_after=491s    (first reading -- REJECTED: exceeds R0 even though 1000 shots
                         were spent; physically inconsistent, superseded by the next
                         line, kept here for provenance rather than quietly dropped)
dashboard_after=391s    (R1) -> delta = 1 s over 1000 shots = 1.0 ms/shot BILLED
# quantisation: the dashboard is whole seconds, so the true delta lies in [1,2) s and
#   the implied billed rate in [1.0,2.0) ms/shot.  A single 1-s decrement is not
#   allowed to carry a 120 000-shot decision on its own.
# corroboration: MS_PER_SHOT_WALL_OBSERVED_2026_09 = 1.0 (288 000 shots in ~285 s of
#   wall time, qcloud_run2.log).  hw_mixedness.py:272-294 documents the 14 ms/shot
#   constant as NOT reproducible from anything on disk and as the pessimistic end of
#   an unverified 1x-14x wall-to-billed multiplier; this delta settles it at 1x.
# decision taken: probe B is priced at the pessimistic 14 ms/shot (MSPS deliberately
#   NOT passed) so no sidecar records a single-sample rate as if measured.  The
#   two-sample rate is (392 - R2) ms/shot over 2000 shots and is what the free
#   wcpick step will be given.
# --- CORRECTION to this probe's sidecar metadata (recorded after the fact) ---
# qcloud_raw_wcprobe_WK_C180_20261015T142737Z.json.probe.json carries
#   power.ms_per_shot = 14.000   power.ms_per_shot_source = "dashboard-measured"
# That label was FALSE.  No --ms-per-shot was supplied for this probe; 14.000 is the
# pessimistic module constant MS_PER_SHOT.  Defect: run_wc_probe handed the
# already-resolved bill['ms_per_shot'] to analyze_wc_probe, so wc_probe_power stamped
# 'dashboard-measured' onto whatever it was given.  billing.ms_per_shot_source in the
# SAME sidecar carries the true label ('pessimistic constant MS_PER_SHOT'), so the file
# contradicted itself -- and that contradiction is the proof, not a matter of opinion.
# Fixed at hw_mixedness.py:3503-3514: the caller's value (None) is now passed through.
# NO MEASUREMENT CHANGES.  w=+0.0118, P(data=00000)=0.0426, z_vs_floor=+1.77, the
# ladder, S*=4000, z(S*)=1.35 and exit=5 are all untouched, because wc_probe_power
# resolves None to the same 14.0 it was given.  Only the provenance string changed.
# The WK_C180_2 probe sidecar will carry the same false label: that process had already
# loaded the pre-fix module when it was launched at 15:04:07Z.
# The genuinely MEASURED rate is the dashboard delta recorded above: 1 s over 1000
# shots = 1.0 ms/shot, in [1.0,2.0) ms/shot once the whole-second quantisation is
# admitted.  That, and not 14.0, is what any decision must be priced at -- but only
# after a second sample corroborates it.
# --- wcpick rehearsals on ONE probe (NOT the decision) ---
# hw_evidence/20261015T162937Z_wcpick.json  mode=DETECTION exit=0 at ms_per_shot=1.0
# hw_evidence/20261015T162938Z_wcpick.json  mode=BOUND     exit=5 at ms_per_shot=14.0
# Both were produced from probe A ALONE (n_probes=1, WK_C180_2 still queued) to test the
# code paths and to price the fork; each record discloses that in n_probes, in `refused`
# (empty) and in its `reason`.  They are SUPERSEDED by the decision taken after probe B
# returns and R2 is read.  What they establish is the shape of the fork, not its answer:
#   billed rate <= 3.008 ms/shot -> S*=20000 -> min_w=0.0117 -> DETECTION (w=0.0118 clears)
#   billed rate >  3.008 ms/shot -> S*=15000 -> min_w~0.0135 -> BOUND
# The measured rate is 1.0 ms/shot, i.e. a factor ~3 below the flip, so the flip is NOT
# sensitive to the quantisation of a single 1-second decrement.  It IS sensitive to a
# reading that had not posted yet -- which is why R2 over a known 2000 shots decides it.
